    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n103474" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τετρά̆-πεδος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>with four surfaces</i> or
				<i>sides, squared</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λίθοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.S.
					20.95
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				42(1).119.14
			</span></i>, al. (Epid.), <i><span class="en">
				Arr.
				<u>An.</u>
				6.29.5
			</span></i> (
				v.l.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τετραπόδου</span>
			), <i><span class="en">
				Hdn.
				8.4.2
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>of four feet</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κλίμακατῷ πλάτειτετράπεδον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plb.
					8.4.4
				</span></i>
			, cf. Orac. ap. <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Aem.</u>
				15
			</span></i>.</div>
